# Tests split by what they would reveal.
#
# The scoring tests stay local: they assert TOP_K, TOP_K_SPLIT,
# TRACK_THRESHOLDS and the emission weights, which is the shape of the reward
# curve written out as a table. The modules themselves are public, but a test
# spells out the edge cases and the exact payouts, which is a shortcut for
# anyone tuning an agent against the mechanism rather than the task.
#
# Everything else is published so CI can run it. Those cover the client, the
# corpus draw, detonation and inference isolation, and reference no scoring
# symbol at all — verified before adding each one here.
#
# `tests/*` rather than `tests/`: git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# directory is excluded, so a negation under `tests/` would silently do nothing.
tests/*
!tests/__init__.py
!tests/test_server_client.py
!tests/test_detonate.py
!tests/test_corpus_fetch_sampling.py
!tests/test_npm_detonation.py
!tests/test_inference_isolation.py

# Validator round records
state/
